        <briefdescription>
<para>Synchronously compacts files and returns messages for <ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_file_store_commit_1af7d78ade944ce09c77fc5c5fa4668881" kindref="member">FileStoreCommit::Commit</ref> or Abort. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Each call creates a dedicated batch writer and restores the latest snapshot for the bucket. Writes one file in file name order, preserving surviving physical row order within each input. Ignores target-file-size; produces no file when all input rows are deleted. Supports deletion vectors; real-time mode and data evolution are unsupported. Requires bucket-append-ordered=false and write-only=false. With deletion vectors enabled, callers must serialize compactions within each partition/bucket, even for disjoint inputs. Do not start another compaction, update deletion vectors or overwrite this partition/bucket until the messages are committed or discarded. Without deletion vectors, compactions of disjoint input files may run concurrently in the same partition/bucket. Overlapping compaction or overwrite may cause commit conflicts. Failures may leave orphan files for later cleanup.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>table_path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The root path of the table. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>branch</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The branch to use; an empty string selects main. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>partition</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Complete partition values; empty for an unpartitioned table. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>bucket</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The bucket containing the input files. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>file_names</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Nonempty set of data file basenames. Files need not be contiguous. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>options</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="structpaimon_1_1_options" kindref="compound">Options</ref> overriding the table options. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>file_system</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The file system; nullptr selects one from options. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>pool</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The memory pool; nullptr uses the default pool. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>executor</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The executor; nullptr uses the default executor. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
